.TH "SOROLENS" "1" "Nov 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
sorolens-tui - Launch an interactive terminal dashboard for tracked contracts


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsorolens tui [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch a full-screen, k9s-style dashboard for the Sorolens API.

.PP
The dashboard shows tracked contracts alongside their live event stream,
invocations, watchdog alerts and storage TTL warnings. Data is refreshed on a
timer (default every 5s) and can be refreshed on demand with "r".

.PP
Key bindings:
  tab / shift+tab   cycle panes
  1-5               jump to contracts / events / invocations / alerts / storage
  j / k, up / down  move the selection
  enter             drill down into the selected contract (or alert target)
  /                 filter the contract list
  r                 refresh now
  q, ctrl+c          quit

.PP
The dashboard talks to the API at --api-url and authenticates with an API key
passed via --api-key or the SOROLENS_API_KEY environment variable.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tui

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP=5s
	Polling interval for live data


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API key for authenticating with the Sorolens API

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Sorolens API base URL

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--network\fP=""
	Stellar network (testnet, mainnet, futurenet, standalone)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--output\fP=""
	Output format (table, json, yaml or jsonl)

.PP
\fB--plugin-api-key\fP[=false]
	When dispatching to a plugin, pass the active profile's API key as SOROLENS_API_KEY (off by default)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Configuration profile name (default: $SOROLENS_PROFILE, then the default profile)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	jq-style path filter applied to structured output (e.g. '.items[].name')

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=10s
	Request timeout


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsorolens(1)\fP
